    "created_at": "2017-10-09T09:37:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-09T09:37:01Z",
    "body": "URLs using \\ in those positions are non-conforming. Just because they work doesn't mean module specifier restrictions need to account for them I think. (Also, who knows, perhaps we might want to make `.\\\\` mean something special there and not invoke the URL parser with it at all.)",
